---
description: Avoid em dashes; use hyphens and normal punctuation in copy
alwaysApply: true
---

# Copy & punctuation

Do not use em dashes (`—`, U+2014) in user-facing copy, README, changelogs, handler messages, or template text.

Prefer:

- **Hyphen `-`** for compounds and simple separators in prose (e.g. `PNG, JPEG, or PDF (max 5 MB)`, `Zion English - %s`). For empty table cells and unset detail fields in code, use `constants.DisplayNotSet` (renders as `-`), not a hardcoded `"-"` literal.
- **Comma, period, or colon** to join or break clauses in prose
- **Pipe `|`** for HTML `<title>` separators when needed (e.g. `Zion English | Admin Portal`)

Do not use en dashes (`–`, U+2013) as a stand-in for em dashes.
